[statement]
Observed; the rule is not yet known. As
`conditions-a-name-completes-are-taken-in-apk-s-table-order`, with `sa` in
place of `ra`, which apk's name table holds after `rb`: installing `n`
completes both conditions, yet apk installs `rb`, then decides `X`, which
`rb` needs, for `hi`, before it installs `sa`, whose dependency `Y` has
`lo` alone. ferrata installs both packages at once, and `lo` with `sa`,
before deciding `X`.

